+# Verification Checklist: create-and-scene
+
+Merged verification plan. `L-*` identifies lead rows and `I-*` implementor rows; combined IDs retain both sources, including when an original row spans several merged behaviors. `C-*` adds definition coverage absent from both checklists. These are planned checks, not recorded passing evidence.
+
+References: ESP = `specs/evolving-scene-presentations/spec.md`; PS = `specs/presentation-skill/spec.md`; PV = `specs/presentation-verification/spec.md`. Paths are relative to this change unless stated otherwise. Broader automated checks are limited to test-plan.md's INT-001, INT-002, E2E-001, and E2E-002. Component checks use synthetic events/controlled fixtures; no check asks an agent to operate the product.
+
+Lead rulings resolve grouped/ungrouped DOM reuse, newcomer behavior rather than wrapper names, resize scaling, and missing-attribution warnings. The final scaling ruling supersedes the earlier minimum-viewport/clipping interpretation: every finite positive available size must fit. Rulings are recorded in `/workspace/home/.agent-runner/projects/-artifacts--runtime-candidate-worktree/runs/audited-implement-change-2026-10-19T03-51-48-100871243Z/output/acceptance-assumptions.md`; none requires a user decision.
