+/*
+ * Presentation-owned styling. The scaffold ships no visual defaults: write the
+ * palette, typography, spacing, borders and shadows for this presentation here,
+ * scoped under the `.deck` class that Talk.tsx puts on the presentation root.
+ *
+ * Hooks the kit emits, to target from this file:
+ *   [data-presentation-header] [data-presentation-marker] [data-presentation-title]
+ *   [data-presentation-caption] [data-presentation-footer] [data-presentation-controls]
+ *   [data-presentation-prev] [data-presentation-next] [data-presentation-mode-toggle]
+ *   [data-presentation-progress-dot] [data-presentation-toc-entry]
+ *   [data-presentation-active]        on the current progress dot / ToC entry
+ *   [data-presentation-attribution]   the "made by and-scene" link
+ *   [data-presentation-entity="<id>"] every scene entity
+ * and the classes Scene.tsx applies: .deck-node .deck-chip .deck-arrow .deck-frame
+ *
+ * Make the active dot / ToC entry visibly different from inactive ones, and make
+ * the attribution legible (at least 11px, not the browser-default link style).
+ */
